---
name: parameterless-def-imported
description: an imported parameterless def is invoked at its bare mention, like a local one
backends: [int, js, v2]
---

# The same rule across an import

`parameterless-def-mention` pins the top-level case and `parameterless-def-local` the local one;
this case exists because the IMPORT path is a third code path in the js emitter, and it was the one
still broken: `zeroParamFns` is filled by the entry module's pre-pass only, so an imported
`def answer: String` mentioned bare emitted `_dispatch(answer, 'length', [])` — the FUNCTION
OBJECT, whose `.length` is its arity. `len-ZERO` where int and native print `len-ok`, a silent
wrong answer at exit 0.

It surfaced as `std-os-doc-import` going red when 3440cab4c re-routed `cwd` through
`declaredBindings`, but the defect predates that commit and needs no std module: this case uses a
plain two-def library, which is also why the second def is here — an alias must register under the
LOCAL name, since that is the name the mention uses.

[answer, greeting as hello](lib/parenless.ssc)

```scalascript
def main() =
  println(if answer.length > 0 then "len-ok" else "len-ZERO")
  println(answer)
  println(hello)
```
